    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start but it's a bit vague for what i need. i want to get more specific with the actual \"vibe\" of the low-tier group. like, when a character walks into a low-tier district, what are the physical markers that scream \"low-tier\"? instead of just \"weathered,\" can we talk about things like skin pigmentation, hair textures, or facial features that might suggest a more rugged or \"unrefined\" lineage compared to the almost perfect, maybe even pale or symmetrical look of the elites? i want to use those physical cues to show the class divide without having to explain it all in dialogue.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
